**How to implement.** A category's name resolves through the categories its caller holds, never through the code seed (001 §B and §R: the code seed values go; the S1.7 brief: they 'resolve through a category list handed in instead (the CategoryProxy's listCategories)', and every caller passes the live store; .spec-md §0.1, `MaterialLibrary.fs` row). Resolution changes here; `standardCategories` itself stays until step 58. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialLibrary.fs`: `tryFindCategory (categories : MaterialCategory list) (id : CategoryId) : MaterialCategory option` and `tryFindCategoryByName (categories : MaterialCategory list) (name : CategoryName) : MaterialCategory option` search the list they are given, and `CategoryId.categoryName` becomes `member this.categoryName (categories : MaterialCategory list) : string`: the found category's name, or the id's GUID string for an id the list does not hold, as today. None of the three reads `standardCategories`; each doc is one to three lines saying the caller passes the live category store's `listCategories` (spec 0050 S1.7). (2) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryFacets.fs`: the material category facet (`materialCategoryDef`) becomes a private function of the categories; `materialFacets (categories : MaterialCategory list) : AttributeDef<MaterialEntry> list` and `libraryFacets (categories : MaterialCategory list) (materials : MaterialEntry list) : AttributeDef<LibraryEntry> list` pass them on; the facet's doc says names resolve through the categories given. Every other facet is unchanged. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/MaterialsWindowView.fs`: `liveCategoryName` answers `id.categoryName` over the store's `listCategories` (`[]` when the listing fails), and `CategoryProxy.liveMaterialFacets` answers `materialFacets` over the same live list. Its override of the category def's `extract` is deleted, because the shared def now resolves live: one resolution, not two. Their docs say so in no more words. (4) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/LibraryWindowView.fs`: `LibraryWindowContext` (`LibraryWindowView.fs:153`) gains `categories : CategoryProxy` with a one-line doc, and `projectionInputs` (`LibraryWindowView.fs:502`) calls `libraryFacets` with the context's live categories (`[]` when the listing fails). `LibraryWindow.fs` puts its constructor's `categories` argument (`LibraryWindow.fs:34`) into the context. (5) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/MaterialEditorView.fs`: the view-only identity label resolves the name through `m.context.categories.listCategories ()` (`[]` when it fails). (6) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/Report.fs`, module `MaterialLibrary`: `dtoToEntry` takes the categories first and resolves the name through `tryFindCategoryByName categories`; `FileName.importMaterials (categories : MaterialCategory list)` and `FileName.exportMaterials (categories : MaterialCategory list) (entries : MaterialEntry list)` pass them on; the DTO doc, the `dtoToEntry` comment and the export's category comment say the categories are the caller's. (7) The callers in the tests pass the fixture's categories (step 41): `materialFacets`, `libraryFacets`, `importMaterials` and `exportMaterials` take `BuiltinCatalogue.categories ()` in `LibraryFacetsTests`, `PolarizerBehaviorTests` and `ExportImportTests`. Every `LibraryWindowContext` record that `LibraryWindowTests`, `LightSourceEditorTests` (`libraryContext`) and `WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests` (`libraryContext`) build gets `categories = BuiltinCatalogue.categoryStore (fun _ -> [])` (step 45), or the fact's own category store where the fact builds one. Every fact keeps its name and its assertions. (8) Facts. `CategoryProxyTests` gains `a category resolves by id and by name through the list it is given`: over `BuiltinCatalogue.categories ()` with Glass renamed to a test-local name, `tryFindCategory` answers the renamed record for `CategoryIds.glass`, `tryFindCategoryByName` finds it by the new name and answers `None` for `Glass`, and `CategoryIds.glass.categoryName` is the new name; over `[]`, `tryFindCategory` answers `None` and `categoryName` the id's GUID string. `LibraryFacetsTests` gains `the category facet names each material's category through the categories it is given`: over `BuiltinCatalogue.materials ()`, the category facet of `materialFacets (BuiltinCatalogue.categories ())` keys Silicon (`MaterialIds.silicon`) by `Semiconductor`, and by the new name when Semiconductor (`CategoryIds.semiconductor`) is renamed in the list handed in. No cache, fallback catalogue or second resolution path is added.

**Acceptance.** After the switch, `tryFindCategory`, `tryFindCategoryByName` and `CategoryId.categoryName` MUST NOT read `standardCategories`, and `Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryFacets.fs` MUST NOT name it; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a category resolves by id and by name through the list it is given` and `the category facet names each material's category through the categories it is given`; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, every renamed-category fact included; and build, elevation and the seven s07 invariants MUST pass.
